 "summary": "Mostly no. On BTC, ETH and SOL, price after CCI(20) went below −100, or crossed back up through −100, was the same as random on 1h, 4h and daily. The one result that holds up is daily CCI(20) crossing up through +100 while the pair was above its 200-day SMA: it beat random by about 5.7% after 20 days, held without its strongest stretch, and showed at 10, 20 and 50 candles.",
 "verdicts": [
  {
   "use": "Buying the dip (below −100 or crossing up −100)",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random on 1h, 4h and daily, both while CCI(20) held below −100 and on the cross back up through −100."
  },
  {
   "use": "Riding a breakout (crossing up +100)",
   "verdict": "fragile",
   "text": "Beat random on daily only because of the run between Jan 1 and Mar 27, 2021, and matched random on 1h and 4h. In uptrends it beat random by about 5.7% and held without its strongest stretch; in downtrends it matched random."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting overbought (above +100)",
   "verdict": "fragile-worse",
   "text": "Worse than random on daily, and the result rests on one SOL stretch between Jan 1 and May 18, 2021. On 1h and 4h it was the same as random."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting the cross down through +100",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random on 1h, 4h and daily, pooled across the three pairs."
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "On 1h, CCI(20) crossing up through −100 gave 7,433 entries in 2,965 separate moves. Twenty candles later they were 0% from random entries, inside a luck band of −0.06% to 0.09%. Holding below −100 enters about four times as often and also matched random. On 4h, both settings stayed inside the band in uptrends and in downtrends.",
  "Daily CCI(20) below −100 looked 4.14% worse than random in uptrends. That rests only on signals on Jan 4–11, 2022, and without them it was the same as random. In downtrends it showed nothing.",
  "Daily CCI(20) crossing up through +100 beat random by 3.13% after 20 days, outside a band of −2.49% to 2.2%. Without the run between Jan 1 and Mar 27, 2021, it falls back to random, and at 100 candles it shows nothing. The uptrend split carries it: above the 200-day SMA it beat random by 5.7% across 72 moves and held without its strongest stretch. Below it, at −2.06%, it was the same as random.",
  "Shorting while daily CCI(20) was above +100 did 4.57% worse than random after 20 days. Its strongest stretch is 72 entries on SOL between Jan 1 and May 18, 2021, and without it the result is the same as random. In uptrends it was 5.26% worse, resting on signals between Jul 30 and Sep 11, 2021; in downtrends it showed nothing. On 1h and 4h it matched random.",
  "Single stretches and single horizons can fake a result. On 1h, the short on a cross down through +100 beat random in uptrends by 0.13%, but only at 20 candles; at 10, 50 and 100 it showed nothing. On BTC 1h the same cross rests on two signals on Dec 3, 2021. On daily in uptrends it looked 4.07% worse, resting on signals between Oct 8 and Dec 28, 2023.",
  "For a long DCA bot, CCI dip timing adds nothing on these pairs, so the DCA orders and take profit do the work. The shape worth testing is daily CCI(20) crossing up through +100 as a filter beside a trend condition, such as price above the 200-day SMA, because in downtrends it matched random. A short bot that opens while daily CCI is above +100 is trading against strength. Leaving that setting out costs nothing on 1h and 4h, where it matched random."
 ],
